#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# spherical_hankel_h2

#% text
# `spherical_hankel_h2(n, z)` gives the spherical Hankel function of the second kind `spherical_bessel_j(n, z) - im*spherical_bessel_y(n, z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 10.47.6. For integer `n` it is `exp(-im*z)` times a polynomial in `1/z`; it describes incoming spherical waves.

#% item
# Machine numbers give numerical values; symbolic arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
spherical_hankel_h2(2, 1.5)
#% output
#= 0.12734928368840825 + 1.3457126936204509im

#% cell
spherical_hankel_h2(1, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.43539777497999166 + 0.35061200427605527im

#% cell
spherical_hankel_h2(0, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8414709848078965 + 0.5403023058681398im

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The mean of the two kinds is the spherical Bessel function:

#% cell
(spherical_hankel_h1(3, 2.5) + spherical_hankel_h2(3, 2.5))/2 - spherical_bessel_j(3, 2.5)
#% output
#= 0.0 + 0.0im

